Before leaving, Asha tells me about Moti's routine.
She explains some strict rules to me.
Asha says, "Maya, you must give him food at exactly eight o'clock."
"At eight in the morning and eight at night."
"You must always put a leash on him in the park."
"You must not let him loose there."
"And the most important rule."
"You must not give him human food at all."
"Do not give him any of our snacks."
Moti looks at me and wags his tail.
I listen to Asha's words carefully.
I reassure her.
I say, "Asha, do not worry at all."
"I have understood all your rules well."
"I will feed him exactly on time."
Asha smiles and says thank you to me.
She strokes Moti's head and leaves.
